    "subject": {
      "description": "A pedestrian street painted in wide rainbow stripes leads toward a tall, pale, ribbed church spire. A large decorative bell woven from evergreen boughs and lights hangs on a wire strung across the street just above head height. A man in a blue jacket and knit cap walks up the rainbow crosswalk toward the camera; a woman in a white puffer coat with a fur-trimmed hood walks past on the right, and shops with string lights line both sides.",
      "media_analyzed": "photo"
    },
    "subject_description": {
      "standard": "Skólavörðustígur, Reykjavík's rainbow-painted pedestrian street, framed toward Hallgrímskirkja church with a giant evergreen Christmas bell strung overhead, as Hans walks up the crosswalk at dusk.",
      "monty_python": "A street has been dyed the full spectrum of the rainbow, apparently to lull tourists into a false sense of Pride-parade security before ambushing them with a fifteen-foot evergreen bell dangling menacingly overhead like the sword of Damocles, if the sword of Damocles smelled of pine needles. A man strides purposefully up the yellow stripe, unaware he is being watched by a Gothic concrete rocket ship at the end of the street, which is, in fact, a church."
    }
