      "monty_python": "Behold: a church built, apparently, by someone who looked at Iceland's volcanic basalt columns and said 'more, but concrete, and taller.' A bronze Viking stands guard out front, cape frozen mid-billow, sword undrawn, silently judging the tourists queuing for the gift shop. The sky, unprompted, performs a tasteful pink watercolor wash in the background, as if the universe itself is trying to upsell the postcard."
